     :last-update "2026-09-22T10:03:50.902048-05:00"},
    :avoid-when
    ["the transformation needs semantic reasoning (translation / paraphrase / domain-shift) — that's NOT deterministic; use :llm"
     "the task is producing new structure from raw text — that's extraction"
     "the input is unstructured — extract first, then transform"
     "the transformation rule is fully specifiable"
     "the transformation feeds another stage that binds on specific fields"],
    :strengths
    [{:trait
      "implement transformations in :code (NOT :llm) when the mapping is deterministic — preserves byte-for-byte fidelity, costs zero tokens, runs in milliseconds",
      :good-when
      "the transformation rule can be expressed as a pure function over the input",
      :recommended-pattern
      "[:code {:reads [:input] :writes [:output] :fn (fn [{:keys [inputs]}] {:output (mapv (fn [r] (select-keys r [:a :b])) (:input inputs))})}]"}
     {:trait
      "for per-item independent transformations over a vector, use :map-each rather than a single batch :code call when the per-item work is non-trivial — supports per-item failure isolation",
      :good-when
      "items can fail independently AND partial success has value",
